# Rust
backend/target/
backend/**/*.rs.bk
# backend/Cargo.lock is tracked on purpose: this is an application, not a
# library, so every build and CI run has to resolve the same dependency
# versions. Without it, two builds of the same commit can differ.

# Node / SvelteKit
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.svelte-kit/
frontend/build/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/dist/

# Env
.env
.env.local
# The deliverable stack's credentials. `.env.prod.example` is tracked (it holds
# placeholders); this one holds real values and must never be committed.
.env.prod
!.env.example

# Playwright
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/blob-report/
frontend/playwright/.cache/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

#skills
.atl/
.codegraph/

#PLAN & features
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose: an unanchored `plan-v1a.md` also
# matched `odd/tasks/plan-v1a.md`, the ODD feature document the subagents read.
# The working plans stay local; the feature document is part of the work.
/PLAN.md
/plan-v1.md
/plan-v1a.md
/plan-v2.md
/plan-v2.5.md
/plan-v3.md

# impeccable was removed on 2026-10-26 (see odd/tasks/plan-v1a.md, L14): the
# skill bundle, its per-machine agents and the .impeccable/ artifacts are gone,
# so the ignore rules they needed are gone with them. The artifacts survive in
# git history at 17e331b. Nothing here hides a tool's state directory any more:
# a directory a tool recreates shows up as untracked, which is what we want.

# Pi project-local agent definitions
/.pi/

# Kate editor swap files (the .gitignore above covers *.swp but not this suffix)
*.kate-swp
